  - name: "Ectoplasmic body"
    description: "Forms, at will and at no I.S.P. cost, a featureless six foot (1.8 m) humanoid body under the orb that can wear clothing and carry objects. Forming one takes two melee rounds; changing form or dissipating it takes two melee actions. If destroyed, no new body can be formed for six hours, and the Dirari loses 10% of its H.P. and 20% of its S.D.C. (round up); only destroying the orb slays it. INVISIBLE VAPOR: seen only by those who see the invisible, with ultraviolet sight, or who see Astral Beings; physical but squeezes through cracks and keyholes; limbs lift no more than 40 lbs (18 kg) and stretch 40 feet (12.2 m) +5 feet (1.5 m) per level, and must be retracted before the body changes. Astral H.P.: body 50 +10 per level, limbs (4) 12 +3 per level; only magic, psionics, magic weapons, Astral Beings and weapons that affect Astral Beings or Entities harm it, with M.D. converted point for point. SOLID ECTOPLASM: a luminous white figure that lifts and carries up to the Dirari''s P.S. maximum; limbs stretch 10 feet (3 m) +3 feet (0.9 m) per level and fit openings the size of a golf ball. M.D.C.: body 100 +5 per level, limbs (4) 25 +2 per level; magic, psionics, magic weapons and astral attacks do full damage, energy weapons half, kinetic attacks none."
  - name: "Damage"
    description: "Bash or ram by the orb: 2D6 S.D.C. Vapor body: strike 1D6 S.D.C., power strike 2D6 S.D.C. (counts as two attacks). Solid body: punch or kick 3D6 S.D.C., power punch 6D6 S.D.C. (counts as two attacks). Mega-Damage only through an M.D. weapon or select psionic powers. The six attacks per melee may be physical or psionic. The +2 parry is with the ecto-body arms, which can parry energy blasts without penalty."
