## Lore

The Dirari are psionic spheroids from a dimension where the laws of nature
run differently. Each is a glowing blue orb the size of a soccer ball that
floats at head height on effortless psionic flight and never touches the
ground. Below it the Dirari can shape a body of ectoplasm, either an
invisible vapor or a luminous, featureless white figure, and dress it in
clothes. The result is unnerving: empty clothing walking about under a
disembodied blue head, which is why so many take them for ghosts. They
are mortal beings, though, and they eat, drink and sense the world much as
humans do.

Most Dirari on Earth are career criminals. They came to test their skills
somewhere new and far from their own authorities, and they find theft,
smuggling, kidnapping, extortion, spying and murder for hire exhilarating.
They have a genius intellect and the psionic might of a Mind Melter, much of
it spent keeping their bodies and their flight going. Humanoids mean little
to them beyond being useful.

They are rare: fewer than two hundred are said to roam North America, all
having come through the Calgary Rift, usually working alone or in pairs and
gravitating to places where a quick buck can be made. They like to lead
gangs, or to serve a promising, charismatic leader, and take a particular
pleasure in helping a fallen Cyber-Knight slide further from grace.

## GM Notes

Pronounced DEER-rarr-ree; also known as Orb Men, Orb Ghosts and Ghost
Spheres. The orb is the size of a soccer ball and the ectoplasmic body 5-6
feet (1.5 to 1.8 m) tall; weight 20 lbs (9 kg). Life span 3D6+85 years;
nobody knows how they mate. They need only about 500 calories of food and
1.5 liters of liquid a day, absorbed by osmosis, and favor salty, spicy
food. Their voice comes hollow and mechanical from inside the orb.

Disposition: mischievous, curious and inquisitive at best; cocky,
aggressive, self-serving, opportunistic and cruel at worst. They will
consider anything for money.

Habitat: anywhere, but drawn to North America: the Coalition ''Burbs, Old
Bones, Kingsdale, MercTown, Ciudad Juarez, New Del Rio, the Barony of
Charity, the Pecos Empire and the Pirate Kingdom of Montreal, 1D4 to a
place. Slave market value unknown; none has been sold on Rifts Earth.

Allies: criminals and evildoers of any race, including dragons, demons, the
Minions of Splugorth, the Black Market, Pecos Bandits, mercenary companies,
slavers, pirates and assassin guilds; Naruni Enterprises and the Federation
of Magic employ some. Enemies: heroes and lawmen, especially Cyber-Knights
and Sky Knights. They admire the Coalition States and deal with crooked CS
and Free Quebec soldiers and police, but avoid the Coalition for fear of
being shot as monsters.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dirari-ecto-man');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dirari-ecto-man';

